load @term/seed/code/automaton/cellular
  find cellular-automaton

# The substrate as a computer: the mesh, a hyperbolic cellular automaton, is itself a universal computer. Each cell
# holds a ternary tone, and the two-step rule (collide, then stream) advances the whole mesh each beat, reversibly. From
# that one local, reversible, deterministic rule, universal computation emerges, the same way it does in the simplest
# Turing-complete cellular automata. So the physics and the computation are one object: the universe computes by
# running its own update rule. The form carries the underlying cellular automaton; the collide-then-stream rule and the
# ternary cell state are the substrate.
form substrate-computer
  link automaton, like cellular-automaton
